---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { site, publisher, legal } from '../../site.config.mjs';
const a = site.address;
const sources = [
  { url: legal.analytics.providerUrl, label: 'Vercel: Web Analytics privacy and compliance' },
  { url: legal.hosting.providerUrl, label: 'Vercel: Privacy Policy' },
];
---
<Doc title="Privacy Policy" path="/privacy" entry="Legal · privacy" published={legal.effectiveDate} reviewed={legal.effectiveDate} legalPage sources={sources}
  description={`How ${site.name} (${site.domain}) handles information about visitors. In short: no accounts, no forms, no cookies, no advertising tracking.`}>
  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>{site.name} is published by {legal.controller} ("we"). We are the controller of personal data processed through this website. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Postal address: {a.organisation}, {a.building}, {a.street}, {a.postalCode} {a.locality}, {a.country}{a.placeholder && ' (placeholder address, to be confirmed)'}.</p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <p>This site has no user accounts, no comment system, no newsletter and no forms. We collect only:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Aggregate usage statistics</strong> through {legal.analytics.provider}. For each page view it may record the time, the page address, the referring page, filtered query parameters, an approximate location (country, region, city) derived from the request, device type, operating system and browser with versions. It does not use cookies. Visitors are distinguished by a hash created from the incoming request, which is discarded after 24 hours. We see only aggregated statistics and cannot identify individual visitors from them.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs</strong> kept by our hosting provider, {legal.hosting.provider}, which receives the technical data every web server receives (such as IP address, browser user agent and the page requested) in order to deliver the site and protect it from abuse.</li>
    <li><strong>Emails you send us</strong> at {site.email}: your address, your message and anything you include in it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Why we use it, and the legal basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Aggregate statistics: to understand which pages are read so we can maintain the reference. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in running and improving the site (EU and UK GDPR Article 6(1)(f); Brazil LGPD Article 7, IX).</li>
    <li>Server logs: to deliver the site securely. Legal basis: legitimate interest, as above.</li>
    <li>Emails: to answer you and, where relevant, to correct the site. Legal basis: legitimate interest, or steps you asked us to take.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information, share it for cross-context behavioural advertising, or use it for automated decisions with legal or similar effects.</p>

  <h2>4. Who receives it</h2>
  <p>{legal.hosting.provider} hosts the site and provides {legal.analytics.provider}, acting as our processor. Emails are handled by {publisher.name}'s email provider. We may disclose information where the law requires it. Some of these providers process data outside your country, including in the United States; where required, transfers rely on appropriate safeguards such as standard contractual clauses.</p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Analytics visitor hash: discarded automatically after 24 hours. Aggregated statistics contain no personal data and may be kept indefinitely.</li>
    <li>Server logs: kept by the hosting provider for the limited period set out in its policy.</li>
    <li>Emails: kept for as long as needed to deal with your message, and no longer than 24 months after the matter is closed, unless the law requires longer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you have rights over your personal data, including to access it, correct it, delete it, restrict or object to its use, and receive a portable copy. Under Brazil's LGPD you may also ask for confirmation that we process your data and for information about who we share it with. California residents have the right to know, delete and correct personal information, and not to be discriminated against for using these rights; we do not sell or share personal information as those terms are defined in California law.</p>
  <p>To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We will answer within one month (or the shorter period your law sets). You may also complain to your data protection authority, for example the Information Commissioner's Office in the United Kingdom, your national authority in the European Union, or the Autoridade Nacional de Proteção de Dados (ANPD) in Brazil.</p>

  <h2>7. Children</h2>
  <p>The site is a general reference and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

  <h2>8. Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Pages link to the {publisher.name} directory, to company websites and to the sources we cite. Those sites have their own privacy policies.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We will update this policy if what we collect changes, and show the new date at the top of the page.</p>
</Doc>
